{"jobId":2605,"title":"Delta One Index Trader","description":"About the company: Top European Bank. Job responsibilities: - Execute and manage Delta One index trading strategies to optimize portfolio performance. - Monitor market trends and analyze data to identify trading opportunities and risks. - Collaborate with research and analytics teams to develop and refine trading models. - Ensure compliance with regulatory requirements and internal risk management policies. - Maintain and enhance relationships with clients and stakeholders to support business growth. - Provide timely and accurate reports on trading activities and market conditions. - Contribute to the development of new trading products and strategies. Job requirements: - Bachelor's degree in Finance, Economics, or a related field; advanced degree preferred. - 1 - 3 years experience in Delta One Index trading, . - Strong understanding of index trading strategies and APAC markets. - Proficiency in trading platforms and financial modeling software. - Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. - Ability to work under pressure and make quick, informed decisions. - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.","expected":{"yoeMin":1,"yoeMax":3,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Delta One Index Trader; '1-3 years' -> yoe 1-3. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2668,"title":"Finance Executive FP&A / Management Reporting Support","description":"Finance Exec (FP&A / Management Reporting Support) Why This Role Is Awesome - Join a Bursa-listed regional group undergoing a finance transformation. - Gain hands-on exposure to Financial Planning & Analysis (FP&A), budgeting, forecasting, and management reporting. - Work closely with a Finance Manager and benefit from strong mentorship. - Clear career progression opportunities into Senior Executive or Assistant Manager roles. Responsibilities - Support monthly management reporting, including data preparation and analysis. - Assist in budgeting, forecasting, and tracking actuals versus budget. - Prepare variance analysis and support narrative/commentary for management reports. - Maintain financial data, schedules, and reporting templates. - Support the preparation of dashboards, KPIs, and flash reports. - Assist with ad-hoc analysis and special projects or feasibility studies. - Work closely with the Financial Reporting team to ensure data accuracy. Must-Have - Degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field. - 1–3 years of relevant finance or reporting experience. - Strong Excel skills and an analytical mindset. - Comfortable working with numbers and large data sets. Nice to Have / Bonus - Exposure to FP&A, management reporting, or budgeting. - Experience in multi-entity or project-based environments. - Familiarity with ERP systems. - ACCA / CIMA papers in progress. Team & Culture - Reports directly to the Finance Manager (Management Reporting & FP&A). - Works closely with Financial Reporting and AP/AR teams. - Fast-paced but supportive environment with structured learning. - Strong emphasis on upskilling and internal mobility. Location - Damansara Heights, Kuala Lumpur - Fully office-based | Monday–Friday","expected":{"yoeMin":1,"yoeMax":3,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Finance Executive FP&A; '1-3 years' -> yoe 1-3.