{"jobId":2671,"title":"Finance Manager Corporate Finance & Special Projects","description":"Finance Manager (Corporate Finance & Special Projects) Why are they awesome? - Public-listed group undergoing finance transformation and expansion, offering visibility across both operational and strategic finance. - Unique hybrid role combining management reporting, corporate finance, and special projects. - Exposure to board-level reporting, feasibility studies, and investment decision-making. - Collaborative culture that encourages cross-functional learning and rotation between reporting and corporate finance functions. - Reports directly to the Senior Financial Controller and works closely with the CFO. Responsibilities: Management Reporting - Lead the preparation and review of management accounts, flash reports, and variance analyses. - Perform quality checks on financial statements from the reporting team and prepare management narratives. - Oversee forecasting, budgeting, and monitoring of actual vs planned spend. - Prepare quarterly board papers, performance dashboards, and executive summaries. Corporate Finance & Special Projects - Build and maintain financial models and valuations for new projects, investments, and acquisitions. - Conduct feasibility and financial viability studies for new business opportunities. - Support fund-raising activities including project financing and equity placement. - Liaise with banks, advisors, and legal teams for due diligence and financial documentation. Must Have: - Degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or related discipline. - 5–7 years of experience in management reporting, corporate finance, or project finance. - Proven experience in financial modeling, valuation, and investment analysis. - Strong command of budgeting, forecasting, and performance management processes. Nice to have / Bonus: - MBA, CFA, or ACCA qualification. - Experience in construction, infrastructure, or project-based industries. - Proficiency in Mandarin to liaise with regional partners and investors. Location: - Damansara Heights, Kuala Lumpur - Modern HQ with a 5-day work week","expected":{"yoeMin":5,"yoeMax":7,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Finance Manager Corporate Finance; '5-7 years' -> yoe 5-7. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2672,"title":"Finance OfficerPayment","description":"About the company: Our client is a leading provider of data management solutions, specializing in cutting-edge technology to optimize data storage and processing. Job responsibilities: -Act as the main point of contact with banks and headquarters for day-to-day financial transactions -Process payments across the APAC region, including bank transfers and H2H payments -Oversee the management of bank and H2H payment accounts -Implement and enhance automation within financial systems -Provide payment-related support to departments such as Order Operations, Delivery, Sales, and GSM -Liaise with banks and payment vendors on behalf of APAC entities -Assist with month-end closing procedures -Support both internal and external audit processes -Assist with bank account openings, KYC compliance, signatory updates, and other administrative requirements -Prepare and manage finance/banking documentation -Carry out additional ad hoc tasks as needed Job requirements: - Bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, or a related field. - Minimum of 2 years of experience in finance or payment processing roles. - Strong understanding of financial regulations and payment processing systems. - Proficiency in financial software and Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel. - Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously. - Effective communication and interpersonal skills.","expected":{"yoeMin":2,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Finance Officer Payment; 'Minimum of 2 years' -> yoeMin 2, max null. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2708,"title":"Global Markets Trade and Communications Surveillance Quality Assurance Specialis","description":"The Market Integrity (MI) Domain and Practices APAC comprises several operating units, including Monitoring and Surveillance, Control Room, MI Framework, and GBFR. These teams are distributed across APAC, with main hubs in Singapore, Hong Kong, and Japan, and support from India and Lisbon for various monitoring and surveillance functions. The MI APAC Monitoring and Surveillance (M&S) teams in Singapore, Hong Kong, and Japan are responsible for monitoring and surveillance of CIB (Global Markets, ALMT, Global Banking and Securities Services (2S)) and IFS (Wealth Management) businesses within APAC. The Front Office Conduct Surveillance (FOCS) team, as part of the target operating model (TOM) on CIB, performs the majority of 1LOD controls. The Quality Assurance (QA) role is integral to the oversight of the CIB Market Surveillance framework, contributing to the continuous improvement and reinforcement of the monitoring process for both Lines of Defence (FOCS Team/1LOD and M&S team/2LOD). The QA team supports the CIB Surveillance program by re-performing controls to review FOCS and M&S’s evaluations of their investigations on trade and communications alerts, ensuring compliance with bank policies, procedures, standards, and regulatory requirements. Key Responsibilities - Conduct targeted Quality Assurance (QA) reviews on first line of defence (FOCS team/1LOD) and second line of defence (M&S team/2LOD) to assess and review compliance with legal, regulatory, and internal Bank policy requirements. - Escalate potential issues and exception items identified during the review process to the Head, Quality Assurance APAC for further discussion and investigation if necessary. - Prepare and distribute reports to Senior Compliance Management detailing review findings and recommendations, and report on significant activities conducted and planned for the upcoming period. - Anticipate regulatory requirements as exemplified in regulatory actions and guidance, ensuring these requirements are met within the APAC surveillance program and implementing compensating controls to manage risk. - Ensure APAC M&S procedures are enhanced to formalize local controls in alignment with Group requirements, including the gathering and evidencing of supporting documentation. - Collaborate with colleagues across FM/MI and other Compliance teams on transversal quality control and assurance-related initiatives. - Propose, develop, and execute new reviews to address emerging trends and identify red flags within the surveillance program. - Mitigate risks of exposure through process change proposals and escalation of recommendations within APAC M&S through MI Management. - Contribute to working groups focused on enhancing controls and the quality of the market surveillance program. - Assist the Head, Quality Assurance APAC with examinations by the Bank’s regulators and internal auditors/IG. - Assist the Head, Quality Assurance APAC with the monitoring and resolution of IG issues. - Conduct investigations and projects as deemed necessary by M&S/MI Management. - Execute the CIB Surveillance Permanent Challenge framework for 1LOD/2LOD in APAC. Technical Competencies - Strong understanding of financial markets products, including practical knowledge of trading activities. - Good understanding of conduct risk and market misconduct concepts. - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to exercise sound and balanced judgement. - Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to communicate and consult at all levels. - Ability to articulate clear findings and recommendations to stakeholders. Behavioural Competencies - Confident in challenging the status quo. - Committed to confidentiality, integrity, and objectivity. - Proactive in identifying risks and proposing solutions. - Ability to handle multiple tasks simultaneously and work within agreed timelines. Experience and Qualifications Required - University graduate with a major in Accounting, Business Administration, Economics, Finance, Law, or equivalent qualification. - Prior experience in CIB activities and Financial Markets. - 5-7 years of experience in the Front Office, Middle Office, or related Control, Audit, or Compliance background relating to Global Markets trading activities or Investment Banking activities.","expected":{"yoeMin":5,"yoeMax":7,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Surveillance QA Specialist; '5-7 years' -> yoe 5-7. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2861,"title":"Manager, Marketing Trader","description":"Manager, Marketing Trader About the Role Apical is seeking a commercially driven Marketing Trader to execute sales and marketing strategies across assigned markets and products. The role focuses on: - Driving volumes and margins - Managing key customer relationships - Identifying growth opportunities - Providing market intelligence to support trading decisions - Exposure to risk management concepts is a plus What You Will Do - Execute trading and marketing strategies to meet volume, margin, and growth targets - Build and grow relationships with customers, distributors, and partners - Identify new commercial opportunities; negotiate pricing and contract terms - Monitor market trends, competitor activity, and supply–demand dynamics - Collaborate with HQ, production, logistics, and marketing teams on go-to-market plans - Provide timely market insights to support commercial decision-making - (Good to have) Apply basic risk management concepts such as exposure, hedging, and counterparty assessment What We Look For - Bachelor’s degree or higher - 8–10 years’ experience in commodities trading/marketing, ideally palm or agri-commodities - Strong commercial acumen and relationship management skills - Good analytical, negotiation, and communication abilities - Familiarity with palm markets preferred; risk management exposure is an advantage Why Join Apical? - Growth & Scale: Be part of one of the world’s leading processors and traders of palm and renewable products - Entrepreneurial Culture: Fast-paced, empowered environment where commercial ideas and initiative are valued - Global Exposure: Work with diverse markets, customers, and teams across the value chain - Impact & Sustainability: Contribute to responsible sourcing, decarbonization, and the future of renewable solutions","expected":{"yoeMin":8,"yoeMax":10,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Manager Marketing Trader; '8-10 years' commodities trading -> yoe 8-10. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2388,"title":"Sales Development Representative, Korea","description":"WHO WE ARE Notion is the collaborative AI workspace where teams and agents think together https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vkpYpWfEK5s. We're building one place where your knowledge, projects, meetings, and AI tools live side by side, so work feels faster, clearer, and less fragmented. Millions of individuals, small teams, and large companies run their work on Notion. Notinos (our employees) are customer zero in bringing this future of work to life. We care about craft, humanity, and building things that last — not just shipping the next feature, but setting a standard for how modern teams (with humans and agents working together) think and execute. ABOUT THE ROLE We're looking for a motivated Sales Development Representative with an entrepreneurial and building spirit to join our founding sales team! As an early member of the team, you'll be instrumental in helping define our sales motion, meaningfully shape our future product, and drive business revenue all while having a blast doing it! WHAT YOU'LL ACHIEVE - Experiment on outbound activity to decision makers with customized messaging and channels to generate Enterprise opportunities - Handle inbound requests from prospective customers interested in buying Notion - Organize and take thorough notes on prospects. - Qualify those prospects to determine whether or not they’re a good fit for Notion - Prospect and develop new potential accounts by educating contacts about how they can increase their team's collaboration, transparency, and productivity with Notion - Hold meetings with prospective customers to understand their business challenges and goals - Help build playbooks and define our sales motion - Hold ownership over pipeline generation tactics and strategic approaches - Learn about our product inside and out and be able to give demos customized to the needs of different personas - Collaborate and influence on performance initiatives, product launches and service innovation when working with cross-functional partners - Work with our Global and Regional Marketing team to build strong program feedback loops - Work with our Global GTM team to hit revenue & pipeline generation targets SKILLS YOU'LL NEED TO BRING - Minimum 3+ years of experience in sales or sales development in SaaS tech or a high-growth environment - Experience making cold calls to decision makers - A track record of high achievement in current and previous roles, hitting or exceeding quotas - Engaging and compelling customer skills - high cognitive empathy and ability to craft stories tailored to the customer - You LOVE talking to customers; Always interested in digging deeper and learning more about their needs - Fluency in Korean and Business level in English NICE TO HAVES - Experience in sales, marketing, business development for enterprise companies in Korea is preferred - You've got strong technical chops — comfort with speaking about technical implementations. - A builder’s mentality who thrives in collaborative environments; Comfort with ambiguity and solutions-oriented mindset - You don’t need to be an AI expert, but you’re curious and willing to adopt AI tools to work smarter and deliver better results. By clicking “Submit Application”, I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s Global Recruiting Privacy Policy https://notion.notion.site/Notion-Global-Recruiting-Privacy-Policy-fc3eb4e829354a26a2bb6fd5e289b550. https://dev.notion.so/a3ce416456924276a59de91bca740028?pvs=21#LI-Onsite A NOTE ON AI You don’t need deep AI expertise for every role, but we do expect every Notino to be intellectually curious, drawn to tinkering and discovery, and excited to use AI as a real collaborator in their work. For some roles, AI fluency is a core requirement — when that’s the case, we’ll make it explicit in the qualifications. People who thrive here don’t treat AI as a novelty. They use it to think better, move faster, and build more creatively. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY & ACCOMMODATIONS We hire talented and passionate people from a variety of backgrounds because we want our teams to reflect the wide diversity of our customers. If you’re excited about a role but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every bullet point listed, we still encourage you to apply. Notion is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Notion considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Notion is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please let your recruiter know.","expected":{"yoeMin":3,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Notion SDR Korea; 'Minimum 3+ years' -> yoeMin 3, max null. No pay in posting -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2469,"title":"Account Executive B2B","description":"Account Executive (B2B) A rapidly growing SaaS company is currently looking for an Account Executive (B2B) to own the full sales cycle and consistently exceed monthly targets across both new business and existing accounts. In this role, you’ll generate opportunities through a mix of inbound and self-sourced leads, engage directly with C-level executives and key stakeholders, and lead impactful product demonstrations (both virtual and in-person). You’ll navigate complex B2B sales processes by building strong internal champions, influencing multiple decision-makers, and closing high-value deals. Working closely with cross-functional teams, you’ll also play a key role in shaping and evolving our sales strategy as new products and features are introduced. Job responsibilities: - Run a full sales cycle and close both new business and install base at or above quota on a monthly cadence - Find new prospects from both inbound and self-sourced leads - Run qualification calls with C-level executives and department leaders - Run online, and occasionally in person, product demonstrations - Sell through internal champions to multiple stakeholders, as well as directly to the C-level - Work collaboratively with the relevant departments to evolve our sales strategy when new features and products are introduced Job requirements: - Minimum 3 years of proven experience in direct sales (selling over the phone, cold calling, presenting, and pitching, preferably B2B in a Software Company. - Extensive experience selling to customers in Indonesia - Comfortable engaging with a diverse array of customers - Consistently over-achieved quota (top 5-10% of the company) in past positions. - Previous Experience in a startup is preferred - Having previously trained in Sales Methodology will be an advantage. - Ability to work in a fast-paced, team environment. - Strong stakeholder management and communication skills (written & verbal) - Strong customer obsession attitude with evidence of taking independent and appropriate decisions for the customer If you are a high-performing B2B sales professional with a proven track record of exceeding quota and closing complex deals, we invite you to apply for this role.","expected":{"yoeMin":3,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Account Executive B2B; 'Minimum 3 years direct sales' -> yoeMin 3, max null. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2607,"title":"Design Manager PMC / Data Centre - CSA & MEP Integration","description":"Design Manager (PMC / Data Centre) – CSA & MEP Integration Location: - Johor Bahru - 1 year contract (extendable) - Quick start date for those with short or no notice period Why You Should Apply: - Lead multi-disciplinary CSA and MEP design coordination for advanced hyperscale data center campuses. - Work directly with a highly experienced Project Director with over 20 years in the industry. - Join a high-growth, privately owned Project Management Consultancy with a 12-year record of commercial success. Key Responsibilities: - Manage the complete design lifecycle, acting as a bridge between global clients, consultancies, and contractors. - Conduct technical constructability reviews to ensure design feasibility. - Resolve complex MEP and structural layout clashes using BIM/Navisworks. - Drive local authority permitting workflows (TNB, DOSH, BOMBA) to secure building clearances and final Certificate of Completion and Compliance (CCC). Requirements: - 8 to 12+ years of experience in technical design management or multi-disciplinary coordination for heavy industrial, utility, or mission-critical data center projects. - In-depth knowledge of Malaysian UBBL codes and local statutory submission processes. - Proven ability to manage complex interfaces between consultants and contractors. About the Company & Team: - Premier global consultancy serving as a strategic partner to the world’s largest technology hyper-scalers across 18 countries. - Diverse, multi-national management team. - Flat local structure that emphasizes agile design execution over corporate bureaucracy. About You: - Experience with top-tier engineering consultancies or tier-1 contractors. - Demonstrated project longevity across the full lifecycle. - Active professional credentials such as BEM, LAM, PMP, or Green Building (GBIF/LEED) certifications are highly valued. How to Apply: - Click the “apply” button to submit your application. - CVs, LinkedIn profiles, or any available information are welcome. - The recruiter is open to sharing more information before you formally apply. - Every applicant or enquiry will receive a reply. Note: - Employment passes, work visas, or overseas relocation support are not available. - Only candidates with work rights in Malaysia will be considered.","expected":{"yoeMin":8,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Design Manager PMC; '8 to 12+ years' -> yoeMin 8, max null (open '+'). No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2860,"title":"Manager of Electrical Engineering","description":"About the company: Our client is a leading provider of cutting-edge data center solutions, specializing in high-performance, energy-efficient, and secure infrastructure. Job responsibilities: - Lead and manage the electrical engineering team to design, implement, and maintain electrical systems for the data center. - Oversee the development of electrical infrastructure, including power distribution, backup systems, and energy efficiency initiatives. - Ensure compliance with industry standards, safety regulations, and company policies in all electrical engineering projects. - Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support the design and construction of new data center facilities. - Develop and manage project budgets, timelines, and resource allocation for electrical engineering initiatives. - Conduct regular performance evaluations and provide mentorship to team members to foster professional growth. - Identify and implement innovative technologies to enhance the reliability and efficiency of electrical systems. - Monitor and analyze system performance, addressing any issues to minimize downtime and optimize operations. - Prepare technical reports, documentation, and presentations for internal and external stakeholders. - Stay updated on industry trends, emerging technologies, and best practices in electrical engineering and data center operations. Job requirements: - Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related field; a Master’s degree is preferred. - Minimum of 7 years of experience in electrical engineering, with at least 3 years in a managerial or leadership role. - Strong knowledge of electrical systems design, power distribution, and energy efficiency in data center environments. - Proficiency in industry standards and codes, such as IEEE, NEC, and NFPA. - Experience with electrical system modeling, analysis, and simulation tools. - Excellent project management skills, including budgeting, scheduling, and resource allocation. - Strong leadership and team management abilities, with a focus on collaboration and mentorship. - Exceptional problem-solving skills and the ability to make data-driven decisions under pressure. - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with diverse teams and stakeholders. - Professional Engineer (PE) license or equivalent certification is highly desirable.","expected":{"yoeMin":7,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Manager of Electrical Engineering; 'Minimum of 7 years' -> yoeMin 7, max null. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2847,"title":"Logistics Admin","description":"Job Responsibilities: - Receive and verify documents to ensure accuracy and completeness. - Verify customer shipping requirements and preferred shipping modes. - Ensure sales orders are issued and billing is completed timely and accurately, with all necessary supporting documents uploaded in the ERP system. - Update documents in Excel and communicate relevant information to the operations team. - Match packing documents with the Shipment Management System (SMS) for consistency. - Perform ERP system tasks such as creating purchase requests, receipts, and stock transfers. - Conduct weekly and monthly cycle count validations and update results into the ERP system. - Communicate with customers via email, Teams, and phone calls to meet and achieve customer requirements. - Liaise with various teams to fulfill customer orders as needed. - Perform ad-hoc tasks as assigned by supervisors and/or managers. Job Requirements: - Diploma qualification. - Proficient in MS Office applications, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. - At least 1 year of experience as a Logistics Admin. - Minimum 1 year of experience working in a warehousing environment. - Ability to adapt to a fast-paced and meticulous work environment. - Willingness and ability to commit to overtime (including weekends and public holidays). Working Hours: - 8:30am to 5:30pm (Monday to Friday) - 8:30pm to 5:30am (Monday to Friday) Working Location: - Work location will be either at 33 Greenwich or 35 Greenwich, with possible rotation between sites if there is a manpower shortage. - Must be able to commit to overtime on weekdays, weekends, and public holidays. - Must be able to commit to a monthly rotating shift schedule. Night Shift Allowance: - $15 per shift","expected":{"yoeMin":1,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Logistics Admin; 'Minimum 1 year' -> yoeMin 1, max null. TRAP: '$15 per shift' is a shift allowance, not base -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
{"jobId":2857,"title":"Machine Operator","description":"Job Title: Machine Operator (设备操作员) Department: Production Department (生产部) Immediate Superior: Production Supervisor (生产主管) Overview of Responsibilities: - Operate machines to perform grinding, laser cutting, and bending work as required. - Cut, bend, or roll sheet metal according to plans, drawings, and process requirements. - Ensure sheet metal materials meet production needs in a timely manner. Responsibilities and Work Assignments: 1. Sheet Metal Cutting Operations - Responsible for sheet metal cutting according to drawings and process requirements. - Correctly measure and mark sheet metal materials as per plan and specifications. - Arrange and adjust cutting order based on production schedule and work arrangements. - Ensure dimensions, angles, and shapes of cut pieces meet technical requirements. - Comply with safety regulations and operating procedures to ensure safety and quality. - Actively participate in improving and optimizing cutting, bending, and rolling processes to enhance efficiency and quality. 2. Workshop Cleanliness and Teamwork - Maintain cleanliness and safety of the workshop area. - Promptly clear away waste and clutter; effectively implement 6S activities. - Participate in team work, actively coordinate and communicate with other positions to ensure smooth production flow. 3. Surface Treatment and Skill Improvement - Keep the working area clean and safe; clean up waste in time and store in hazardous waste cabin. - Participate in teamwork and coordinate with other positions to ensure smooth production in the sheet metal workshop. - Actively participate in improving and optimizing surface treatment technology. - Participate in training and learning to improve skills. Authority: - Manage property used within the team and be responsible for its safety. - File complaints if there are doubts about the plan or process. - Have the right and obligation to participate in the optimization and improvement of material cutting, bending, rolling processes, and safety. Work Collaborative Relationships: Internal Coordination: - Welding team - Warehouse - Surface treatment team External Coordination: - Not involved Appointment Qualifications: Educational Level: - High school and above (technical school, vocational secondary school preferred) Profession: - Not specified Work Experience: - More than 1 year of experience operating band saws, laser cutting machines, shears, and bending machines. Knowledge/Skills: - Familiar with operation of band saws, laser tube cutting machines, laser plate cutting machines, shears, bending machines, and rolling machines. - Familiar with mechanical drawing. Appraisal Indicators: - Completion rate of the order plan ≥90% - One-time inspection pass rate of the product is 90% - No unqualified matters in on-site 6S activities - No safety accidents occur every month - Daily spot inspection and maintenance of equipment without omissions - Job skills 100% meet the standard N/A for fields without relevant information.","expected":{"yoeMin":1,"yoeMax":null,"salaryMin":null,"salaryMax":null,"salaryCurrency":null,"salaryPeriod":null},"notes":"Machine Operator; 'More than 1 year' -> yoeMin 1, max null. No pay -> salary null (ABSENT)."}
