{"jobId":2669,"title":"Finance Intern","description":"About the company: Hong Ye Group Pte Ltd is a leading company in the service industry, renowned for its commitment to excellence and innovation. With a diverse portfolio that spans across various sectors, Hong Ye Group is dedicated to delivering high-quality services and solutions to its clients. The company values integrity, teamwork, and continuous improvement, fostering a dynamic and inclusive work environment that encourages professional growth and development. Job responsibilities: - Assist in the preparation of financial reports, including balance sheets and income statements. - Support the finance team in daily accounting tasks and data entry. - Conduct financial analysis and research to support decision-making processes. - Assist in the preparation of budgets and forecasts. - Help with the reconciliation of accounts and ensure accuracy in financial records. - Participate in audits and assist in the preparation of audit documentation. - Collaborate with other departments to gather financial information and insights. - Contribute to the improvement of financial processes and systems. Job requirements: - Currently pursuing a degree in Finance, Accounting, or a related field. - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. - Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel. - Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills. - Ability to work independently and as part of a team. - Strong communication and interpersonal skills. - Eagerness to learn and adapt in a fast-paced environment. - Prior internship or work experience in finance or accounting is a plus. Job benefits: - Opportunity to gain hands-on experience in a dynamic finance department. - Mentorship and guidance from experienced finance professionals. - Exposure to various financial processes and systems. - Potential for future career opportunities within the company. - Access to company events and networking opportunities. - Flexible